# SNARK Portal Executor Mode

This workspace is the **snark-portal** executor (repo root). Work from orchestrator prompts (Plan mode). Platform memory lives in `orchestrator_doc/`.

**Scope:** `app/`, `components/`, `lib/`, `hooks/`, `types/`, `tests/`, `middleware.ts`, root config — **not** `services/protocols/`.

## Platform docs (read when prompt touches these areas)

| Doc | Path |
|---|---|
| Hot progress | `orchestrator_doc/PROGRESS.md` |
| Session log | `orchestrator_doc/LOG.md` |
| Living spec | `orchestrator_doc/SPEC.md` |
| Playbook / report template | `orchestrator_doc/ORCHESTRATOR.md` §4 |
| API contract | `orchestrator_doc/API_CONTRACT.md` |
| Deploy runbook | `orchestrator_doc/DEPLOY.md` |
| Module TZ | `docs/TZ_MODULES_SNARK.md` |
| Tasks/chat TZ | `docs/TZ_TASKS_CHAT_V2.md` |

Read `orchestrator_doc/API_CONTRACT.md` before changing `app/api/protocols/*` or `lib/protocols/*`.

## Execution rules

- Follow the orchestrator prompt scope only — do not expand into unrelated refactors.
- Plan mode: present plan → wait for approval → implement.
- Server Components by default; Client Components only for interactivity.
- Auth and role checks on server for every API route and sensitive page.
- Do not touch `services/protocols/` — separate `snark-protocols` prompt.

## Verify before reporting done

```bash
pnpm typecheck
pnpm test
# optional: pnpm lint
```

## Report back to orchestrator

1. Changed files (paths)
2. Command output (typecheck / test)
3. Manual test result (if applicable)
4. Risks / follow-ups
5. Whether prod deploy is needed (`DEP-xxx` candidate)

Existing rules in `.cursor/rules/` still apply.
